WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.735
Hey Gregory. Is it true you have
a saucy secret?

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.905
I-- I actually don't know
what you're talking--

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.441
Do you like to do
your house chores in the nude?

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.243
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.711
NICHOLAS BRAUN:
<i> In episode two, Greg--
 he's got a bunch of lines</i>

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.114 line:0%
in his head about,
this is how I stay neutral.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.115
I'm just an observer.

00:00:16.181 --> 00:00:18.050
I'm not a part
of this necessarily.

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:20.386 line:0%
And it's also a way
of you hedging your bets.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:21.687
-What about the papers?
-GREG:<i> I don't--</i>

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.855
I maybe don't even know

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.357
what they are
or where they came from.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.524
There's a nice agreement

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.027
without it being
an obvious agreement.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.562
It's like, we're both gonna
shut the hell up here, right?

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.731
Fine, okay. Well, we'll
have to see if he buys that.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.399
BRAUN:
<i>The whole relationship is about,</i>

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.134
"What can I trade you?
What can you trade me?"

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.103
Did you know that Shiv's
over there?

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.304
What, at Kendall's?

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.274
What is your fucking game?

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.275
Why? What's yours?

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.744
JESSE ARMSTRONG:
<i> The episode itself came
 out of that question of,</i>

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.814 line:0%
"Why don't they go for Logan
when it feels so possible?

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.915 line:0%
What are their choices?"

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.116
KENDALL ROY:
Uh, it's pretty simple.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.051
Let's gang up on dad
and take him down.

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:53.820
Jesus,
let me shut the door first!

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:57.089
It's quite an alluring,
but quite a terrifying power

00:00:57.122 --> 00:00:58.958
for kids to have
over their father.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:01.227
<i> And so, I thought
 of each character.</i>

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.930
They've all just got really
good reasons to go for him

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.765
<i> and they've all got reasons
 not to.</i>

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.667
JEREMY STRONG:<i> Jesse writes
 in gray areas</i>

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:11.470
so, in a sense, we're all
on our own in this family.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.772 line:0%
And then, in another sense,

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.940 line:0%
we're deeply connected
and enmeshed.

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:16.276
Where are you at?

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.911
Just, uh,
hear him out and report.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.414 line:0%
I think Roman is fully
in dad's court

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.583
<i> 'cause if we banded together
 and got rid of dad,</i>

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.651
there's an uncertainty as to
who's in charge

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.420
and I will not work
for my siblings.

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.122
I can oversee us as CEO on paper

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.257
as we shift
to these spheres of influence

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.592
and evaluate what is core
as we move forward.

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:34.961
So, you'll oversee us?

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:38.031
But it's all very complicated
'cause I feel for my brother.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.698
There's still something there.

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:42.168
Look, guys.
He was gonna send me to jail.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.704
But also,
Shiv's got some sort of agenda.

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:48.607 line:0%
Shiv's kinda positioning
long enough until, you know,

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.476 line:0%
what the greater mass is doing.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.178
If she's gonna push him
off course,

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.380
I should be there too
because then, we did it.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.483
Or if she's jumping ship,

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.318
then I can report that
and that's a win.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.852
Or I can jump ship too
and it's a win.

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:02.021
It's all sorts of win.
Win, winny, win, win, win.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:03.489
I think there's lots of ways
for him to win.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.224
Dad sent doughnuts.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.392
What the fuck?

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.993
I always like the feeling

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:11.397
of language being so important
in our arguments,

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:14.133
<i> but then, there being
 bigger forces at work.</i>

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.635
Something as innocuous
as doughnuts. It means so much.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.803 line:0%
It means you're children.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.372
He wants us all to have
a nice tea party.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.742 line:0%
He may not have even known
about the doughnuts.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.843
He's gonna know.
Of course he is.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:27.514 line:0%
I think it's to do with
making sure they're fed.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.916 line:0%
(CHUCKLING) I think it's
a caring gesture.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.884
They're in a little bit of
a Garden of Eden

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.752
<i> and it's a bit like
 the doughnuts are God saying,</i>

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:34.754
<i> "I see you there</i>

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.655
and you're all naked
and you're all disgusting."

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.224
<i> And just being seen is enough</i>

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.225
to change how you feel
very dramatically.

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.528
How diabolical is that?
(LAUGHTER)

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.431
Con, stop looking
at the fucking doughnuts, man.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:49.935
The old man is indestructible
and Kendall is just fragile.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:50.903
He's also volatile.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.338
Is it the goddamn doughnuts?

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.073
Have you been spooked
by fucking doughnuts?

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.275
That's pathetic, Shiv.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.177
But behind all anger is fear.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.278
You're a fucking prick!

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.214
-Thanks for meeting in person.
-Goodnight. Goodnight!

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:05.184
I had expectations of things
going a certain way for me...

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.084
What?!

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:10.689
...but we're a family that has
a lot of conflict and tension

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:14.260
<i> and if that has been
part of your identity structure,</i>

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:17.263
I think there's a need
for that opponent.

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:19.465
I think I need to get
back to the city.

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:23.469
People need to see
a little family unity.

